      "html": "<ul><li>A daily banksman and plant movement check is a short Yes, No or N/A walk at the start of each shift.</li><li>It confirms that vehicle routes, reversing areas, signals and the banksman's position are safe before plant moves.</li><li>The site manager or the person on the job does it, every working day.</li><li>HSE says banksmen &quot;should only be used in circumstances where other control measures are not possible&quot;, and must be trained and authorised (HSE, checked 17 November 2026).</li><li>Quickler is not training. It records the check and writes it up.</li></ul>"
